# Kerning (reference/common/typography.md): page of 200 × 200 with margins of 20, page area of 160 × 160 from (20, 20).
# Size 24 with Line height 30; with the test metrics each character measures 12 pt with or without kerning, so the
# kerning does not change the layout: each text is one line of 30, 160 wide, one after the other. The image shows the
# same words with the pairs of IBM Plex Sans (A-V, V-A, A-T, T-A, T-o and o-f, all of them closer) and without them.
#   plain:     without Kerning. y = 20.
#   kerned:    Kerning true. y = 50.
#   ligatures: Kerning and Ligatures true: the pair is o and the fi ligature. y = 80.
#   spaced:    Kerning true with Letter spacing 2: each pair also carries the letter spacing. y = 110; 10 spacings of
#              2 make the line 11 × 12 + 20 = 152 wide, which still fits.
#   run:       Kerning true with the first A in bold (Markup: markdown): A-V is not a pair. y = 140.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 200
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 24
				Line height: 30
	Section:
		Text: AVATAR Tofi
			Id: plain
		Text: AVATAR Tofi
			Id: kerned
			Typography:
				Kerning: true
		Text: AVATAR Tofi
			Id: ligatures
			Typography:
				Kerning: true
				Ligatures: true
		Text: AVATAR Tofi
			Id: spaced
			Typography:
				Kerning: true
				Letter spacing: 2
		Text: **A**VATAR Tofi
			Id: run
			Typography:
				Kerning: true
				Markup: markdown
